merlin: Ser Percivel, it's certainly been a while, hasn't it? I had a feeling you would return. There's so much left for us to do, we have no choice but to linger here until it is complete. What exactly prompted your return?
I was followed by a kingfisher. Its persistence made me think it was an omen of some kind.
merlin: That could very well be the case. It isn't difficult to connect such an animal to the Fisher King of our past. Yours, most specifically, though I was under the impression that Galahad had closed that chapter.
Yeah, I thought so too, but here I am. I don't suppose you've noticed any omens of your own?